Without a stub the declared argv is genuinely executed and its stdout is spliced into the render: the
literal prefix can only appear because the format argument reached `date`, and the year behind it is
wildcarded because it is a clock reading, not a contract.

-- fixtures/cwd/probe.md.j2 --
stamp {{ macro('core.macros.date', '+booped-%Y') }}
-- cmd --
booping render /proc/self/cwd/probe.md.j2
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
stamp booped-[..]
-- stderr --
